Let $c \in \{0, \ldots, p-1\}$ be such that for infinitely many $k \in \mathbb{N}$, $c_k = c$.  We see that there exists a thick set $H \subseteq \mathbb{N}$ such that $(p \mathbb{N} + c) \cap H \subseteq R(x,U)$.  Since $p$ was an arbitrary prime greater than $\ell$, we see that the set $R(x,U)$ contains a set of the form in \cref{rem:combinatorial_primes} and hence is dynamically thick, as desired.

